  <section class="lp-section" id="keep-apollo"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">03 / Diagnose the gap</p><h2>Do you need a new database,<br>or another route to the buyer?</h2><p>If the list fits and your workflow works, test the missing data first. A second source should add useful coverage. Paying twice for the same records achieves very little.</p></div>
    <div class="aa-decision-grid">
      <div><h3>Keep Apollo and fill the gaps.</h3><p>Apollo's waterfall enrichment can check other sources after its own database. Compare that route with an external provider on the same missing contacts. Review actual charges: source settings and extra verification can change the bill.</p><p>You may still have a useful company number. Apollo provides HQ numbers without using phone credits. Personal phone results can be mobile, work-direct, home or another type. Preserve that distinction.</p><p>Use our <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/">mobile vs company numbers guide</a> to decide which route deserves the next call.</p><p class="lp-sources"><a href="https://knowledge.apollo.io/hc/en-us/articles/34071089002509-Waterfall-Enrichment-Overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apollo waterfall overview ↗</a> · <a href="https://knowledge.apollo.io/hc/en-us/articles/31969477982221-Access-a-Prospect-s-Phone-Number" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apollo phone types and credits ↗</a></p></div>
      <div id="free-alternatives"><h3>Free Apollo alternatives: check the phone allowance.</h3><p>A free trial can help you reject a poor fit. It rarely funds a full calling campaign. Check how many phone results the allowance can cover after emails, searches and exports.</p><p>Clay's free tier excludes phone enrichment. A phone-enabled paid plan can therefore be the relevant comparison even when a free plan is advertised.</p><p>If a trial cannot cover 25 contacts, use a smaller identical sample for both tools. Record the limit. Use the findings as an initial buying check.</p><p class="lp-sources"><a href="https://www.clay.com/faq/what-features-are-included-in-the-new-plans-how-do-i-pick-the-right-plan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Clay plan features and phone access ↗</a></p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="lp-small">Considering Sales Navigator alongside Apollo? Compare <a href="/resources/linkedin-sales-navigator-lead-generation/">Sales Navigator and Apollo for lead generation</a> to decide whether deeper research earns the extra subscription.</p>
    <div class="aa-switch" id="before-cancelling"><h3>Before you cancel Apollo, check what moves with you.</h3><ul><li><strong>The records:</strong> company and contact IDs, phone types, source details and fields you rely on.</li><li><strong>The next action:</strong> notes, ownership, scheduled callbacks, sequence status and stop requests.</li><li><strong>The workflow:</strong> a tested import, CRM mapping, deduplication and a working calling route.</li><li><strong>The agreement:</strong> export rights, renewal notice, unused credits and the full replacement bill.</li></ul><p>For software you still need after the move, compare our <a href="/resources/best-crm-for-outbound-sales/">outbound CRM guide</a> and <a href="/resources/best-cold-calling-dialers/">cold calling dialler guide</a>.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-small">Also reconsidering the CRM connected to Apollo? Our <a href="/resources/hubspot-alternatives/">HubSpot alternatives guide</a> covers upgrade costs, replacement plans and moving your sales history.</p>
    <div class="lp-note"><strong>Our view: work the list before blaming the database.</strong><p>If suitable accounts remain uncalled or promised callbacks are overdue, fix that first. Review the targeting, the data and the calling separately before adding another subscription.</p></div>
  </div></section>

